---
<ArticleLayout
  title="What Size Generator for a 2,000 Sq. Ft. House? Start With the Loads"
  description="Square footage does not determine generator size. Compare how HVAC, electric heat, pumps, fuel, and selected circuits change a 2,000-square-foot home's backup plan."
  category="Sizing" categoryHref="/sizing/" updated="2026-10-04" verified="2026-10-04" readingTime="6 min read" toc={toc}
  takeaways={[
    'A 2,000-square-foot home has no single generator size: loads and equipment vary substantially between houses of the same area.',
    'Central air, electric resistance heat, well pumps, electric water heating, and desired simultaneous loads can materially change the project.',
    'Use square footage only as context; final capacity must be based on exact equipment data and a site-specific professional assessment.',
  ]}
  sources={[
    { label: APPLIANCE_WATTAGE_SOURCE.label, href: APPLIANCE_WATTAGE_SOURCE.url, type: 'Manufacturer', verified: APPLIANCE_WATTAGE_SOURCE.checkedOn },
    { label: 'Generac: What size generator do I need?', href: 'https://www.generac.com/resources/home-management/what-size-generator-do-i-need/', type: 'Manufacturer', verified: '2026-10-04' },
    { label: 'Generac G0073270 official specification sheet', href: 'https://productmanuals.generac.com/api/manualfiles/G0073270/A0005151077/0', type: 'Manufacturer', verified: '2026-10-04' },
  ]}
  related={[
    { href: '/sizing/what-size-generator-do-i-need/', title: 'Load-based sizing guide', description: 'Plan from actual loads, motor starts, fuel, and transfer equipment.', category: 'Sizing' },
